From 436f9266dad60afaf9ad5b8d213f71856ea5e9a9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 05:15:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Stage the vendored Cap'n Proto C++ licence for packaging

setup.py's build_ext statically links a from-source build of Cap'n
Proto C++ (buildutils/bundle.py, pinned to capnproto-c++-1.4.0, MIT)
into the compiled extension, but setup.cfg's license_files glob names
only pycapnp's own LICENSE.md, so no built wheel -- on any platform --
carries the licence text for the statically-linked library it ships.

Add LICENSE.capnp to the glob; the RISE build stages the upstream
capnproto LICENSE.txt at that path before the wheel is built.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [not exercised by upstream's own build, which never stages a LICENSE.capnp file; needed for RISE's own license-compliance check on statically-linked dependencies]

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 setup.cfg | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/setup.cfg b/setup.cfg
index 04ef73c..a4db8f9 100644
--- a/setup.cfg
+++ b/setup.cfg
@@ -1,3 +1,5 @@
 [metadata]
 description_file = README.md
-license_files = LICENSE.md
+license_files =
+    LICENSE.md
+    LICENSE.capnp
